This directory carries binary inputs that must be included in the Debian
source package. It intentionally contains no OFD implementation source.

On a connected preparation host, download and import the v1.1.0 release:

    debian/scripts/import-ofd-oxt

The script downloads from:

    https://github.com/fanta0625/libreoffice-ofd-extension/releases/download/v1.1.0/ofd-extension.oxt

For this private repository, install GitHub CLI and run gh auth login with an
account that has repository access. The script prefers gh when available;
curl or wget are fallbacks for publicly accessible releases. Failed downloads
do not replace existing inputs. An already downloaded OXT can also be imported
with:

    debian/scripts/import-ofd-oxt /path/to/ofd-extension.oxt

Commit the resulting ofd-extension.oxt and its .sha256 file.
debian/source/include-binaries makes the binary OXT part of the 3.0 (quilt)
source package; the text checksum is included with the other debian/ files.
The normal package build verifies the digest and rejects OXT archives that
contain common implementation-source file types.
